WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.958 --> 00:00:35.958
<b>Arjuna asked what compels a person</b>
<b>to commit sins even against their will.</b>

2
00:00:35.958 --> 00:00:42.750
<b>In the previous verse, Krishna answered that it</b>
<b>is desire or lust that drives such actions.</b>

3
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:48.458
<b>In the following verses, Krishna will </b>
<b>explain where this desire resides,</b>

4
00:00:48.458 --> 00:00:51.500
<b>how it influences us,</b>

5
00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.583
<b>and how to overcome it.</b>

6
00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:57.583
<b>In this thirty-eighth verse of the third chapter,</b>

7
00:00:57.583 --> 00:01:04.000
<b>Krishna describes how desire veils our soul.</b>

8
00:01:08.708 --> 00:01:14.083
<b>Krishna explains that just as </b>
<b>fire can be covered by smoke,</b>

9
00:01:14.083 --> 00:01:19.583
<b>a mirror by dust, and an embryo by the womb,</b>

10
00:01:19.583 --> 00:01:24.958
<b>similarly, the soul becomes veiled by</b>
<b>different layers of desire.</b>

11
00:01:24.958 --> 00:01:29.291
<b>How desire covers our wisdom at different levels</b>

12
00:01:29.291 --> 00:01:32.833
<b>is beautifully illustrated through </b>
<b>these three examples.</b>

13
00:01:32.833 --> 00:01:34.333
<b>First Example -</b>

14
00:01:34.333 --> 00:01:36.750
<b>Fire covered by smoke.</b>

15
00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:41.750
<b>Even when shrouded in smoke, </b>
<b>fire can still perform its function</b>

16
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:43.458
<b>and continue to burn.</b>

17
00:01:43.458 --> 00:01:50.375
<b>Moreover, a slight breeze is enough </b>
<b>to disperse the smoke.</b>

18
00:01:50.375 --> 00:01:56.750
<b>Similarly, one who is only lightly veiled by desire </b>
<b>still has the spiritual fire burning within,</b>

19
00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:03.250
<b>and the thin smoke of desire around </b>
<b>them isn't difficult to remove.</b>

20
00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:07.125
<b>Such a person can comprehend </b>
<b>spiritual knowledge.</b>

21
00:02:07.125 --> 00:02:08.541
<b>Second Example -</b>

22
00:02:08.541 --> 00:02:10.833
<b>A mirror covered by dust.</b>

23
00:02:10.833 --> 00:02:18.208
<b>While a dusty mirror cannot show a </b>
<b>clear reflection, it can still show basic shapes.</b>

24
00:02:18.208 --> 00:02:23.000
<b>A person moderately affected by desire is similar.</b>

25
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:29.541
<b>Such a person cannot clearly perceive the </b>
<b>reflection – that is, the depths of spiritual truth – </b>

26
00:02:29.541 --> 00:02:35.916
<b>yet their intellect can still certainly </b>
<b>function in life's everyday activities.</b>

27
00:02:35.916 --> 00:02:37.416
<b>Third Example -</b>

28
00:02:37.416 --> 00:02:40.000
<b>An embryo in the womb.</b>

29
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:46.375
<b>An embryo covered in the womb cannot </b>
<b>develop, see, or move its limbs.</b>

30
00:02:46.375 --> 00:02:48.000
<b>It is helpless.</b>

31
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.000
<b>Similarly,</b>

32
00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:54.166
<b>one deeply shrouded in </b>
<b>desire is spiritually helpless,</b>

33
00:02:54.166 --> 00:02:57.416
<b>and their intellect cannot function properly.</b>

34
00:02:57.416 --> 00:03:02.416
<b>Krishna is explaining that </b>
<b>desire is everyone's enemy,</b>

35
00:03:02.416 --> 00:03:06.416
<b>though its influence varies at different levels.</b>

36
00:03:06.416 --> 00:03:10.250
<b>What happens if dust isn't cleaned from a mirror?</b>

37
00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.958
<b> The layer of dust grows thicker.</b>

38
00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:13.958
<b>What happens</b>

39
00:03:13.958 --> 00:03:19.500
<b>if smoke accumulates where </b>
<b>there's no gentle breeze of knowledge?</b>

40
00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:21.833
<b>The smoke becomes denser.</b>

41
00:03:21.833 --> 00:03:23.666
<b>The message is clear –</b>

42
00:03:23.666 --> 00:03:29.875
<b>if the layer of desire isn't removed, </b>
<b>it only grows deeper.</b>

43
00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:36.666
<b>The more desire increases, the more </b>
<b>one's spiritual wisdom becomes clouded.</b>

44
00:03:36.666 --> 00:03:42.916
<b>Eventually, like an embryo in the womb, </b>
<b>one becomes helpless.</b>

45
00:03:42.916 --> 00:03:46.666
<b>Desire destroys human consciousness.</b>

46
00:03:46.666 --> 00:03:50.375
<b>Desire pushes us toward the illusion</b>

47
00:03:50.375 --> 00:03:52.958
<b>that our existence is merely this body, </b>

48
00:03:52.958 --> 00:03:56.916
<b>made for trivial material pleasures.</b>

49
00:03:56.916 --> 00:04:00.375
<b> Yet the truth is that we are all souls,</b>

50
00:04:00.375 --> 00:04:04.875
<b>meant for spiritual elevation.</b>

51
00:04:09.333 --> 00:04:11.708
<b>Imagine</b>

52
00:04:11.708 --> 00:04:16.041
<b>that you are walking on life's path as you move,</b>

53
00:04:16.041 --> 00:04:20.375
<b>and in the atmosphere lies a gentle mist.</b>

54
00:04:20.375 --> 00:04:23.791
<b>This mist isn't a hindrance,</b>

55
00:04:23.791 --> 00:04:28.458
<b>as you can still see your way</b>

56
00:04:28.458 --> 00:04:31.375
<b>and continue moving forward.</b>

57
00:04:31.375 --> 00:04:32.958
<b>But</b>

58
00:04:32.958 --> 00:04:39.458
<b>as this mist grows thicker, </b>
<b>your pace begins to slow.</b>

59
00:04:39.458 --> 00:04:41.208
<b>And finally,</b>

60
00:04:41.208 --> 00:04:44.500
<b>when the mist completely engulfs you,</b>

61
00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:49.125
<b>you cannot take even a single step forward.</b>

62
00:04:49.125 --> 00:04:52.125
<b>You must halt there.</b>

63
00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:57.916
<b>Your mind will remain disturbed </b>
<b>until the mist clears.</b>

64
00:04:57.916 --> 00:04:59.416
<b>Similarly,</b>

65
00:04:59.416 --> 00:05:06.375
<b>if desires, especially intense ones, </b>
<b>are left unchecked,</b>

66
00:05:06.375 --> 00:05:10.958
<b>the fog of passion grows denser.</b>

67
00:05:10.958 --> 00:05:18.291
<b>And one loses sight of the spiritual path.</b>

68
00:05:18.291 --> 00:05:21.500
<b>Let's understand this another way.</b>

69
00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:33.416
<b>Small desires are like wisps of smoke </b>
<b>that don't completely block your vision.</b>

70
00:05:33.416 --> 00:05:36.916
<b>They don't confuse you.</b>

71
00:05:36.916 --> 00:05:39.000
<b>For instance –</b>

72
00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:43.208
<b>the desire for new clothes or good food.</b>

73
00:05:43.208 --> 00:05:44.791
<b>These are desires,</b>

74
00:05:44.791 --> 00:05:49.166
<b>but they don't control you.</b>

75
00:05:49.166 --> 00:05:54.500
<b>However, when desires grow stronger,</b>

76
00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:58.833
<b>they become like dust settled on a mirror,</b>

77
00:05:58.833 --> 00:06:03.041
<b>visibly affecting your life.</b>

78
00:06:03.041 --> 00:06:04.833
<b>For example,</b>

79
00:06:04.833 --> 00:06:10.333
<b>buying a new car or house just to show others,</b>

80
00:06:10.333 --> 00:06:12.250
<b>and in this race,</b>

81
00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:17.958
<b>completely neglecting your spiritual growth.</b>

82
00:06:17.958 --> 00:06:22.583
<b>You're merely running from one thing to another.</b>

83
00:06:22.583 --> 00:06:27.625
<b>And if these desires become more intense,</b>

84
00:06:27.625 --> 00:06:35.125
<b>you might find yourself trapped in their web,</b>

85
00:06:35.125 --> 00:06:41.375
<b>helpless like an unborn child in the womb.</b>

86
00:06:41.375 --> 00:06:43.250
<b>You know</b>

87
00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:49.833
<b>these desires are harmful, </b>
<b>yet you cannot stop yourself.</b>

88
00:06:49.833 --> 00:06:51.333
<b>For instance,</b>

89
00:06:51.333 --> 00:06:55.250
<b>addiction to substances or bodily pleasures.</b>

90
00:06:55.250 --> 00:07:02.041
<b>Such desires have no logic behind them, </b>
<b>only compulsion.</b>

91
00:07:02.041 --> 00:07:03.291
<b>Before</b>

92
00:07:03.291 --> 00:07:09.791
<b>desires intensify and ultimately </b>
<b>ensnare you in their web,</b>

93
00:07:09.791 --> 00:07:13.750
<b>it's essential to control them.</b>

94
00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:17.416
<b>Keep asking yourself periodically –</b>

95
00:07:17.416 --> 00:07:22.041
<b>why do you want what you want?</b>

96
00:07:22.041 --> 00:07:29.333
<b>Is it your personal goal, </b>
<b>or are you acting out of envy?</b>

97
00:07:29.333 --> 00:07:33.541
<b>Is it having any negative impact on your life?</b>

98
00:07:33.541 --> 00:07:35.041
<b>And finally,</b>

99
00:07:35.041 --> 00:07:40.458
<b>are you harming anyone else through this?</b>

100
00:07:40.458 --> 00:07:45.458
<b>These questions will keep you </b>
<b>from straying from your path.</b>

101
00:07:45.458 --> 00:07:47.333
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

102
00:07:51.416 --> 00:07:53.500
<b>I hope</b>

103
00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:55.833
<b>that in this verse,</b>

104
00:07:55.833 --> 00:07:59.125
<b>you have understood these rising levels of desire</b>

105
00:07:59.125 --> 00:08:04.166
<b>through metaphors of the smoke </b>
<b>that covers fire, dust gathered on the mirror,</b>

106
00:08:04.166 --> 00:08:05.208
<b>and</b>

107
00:08:05.208 --> 00:08:13.083
<b>and the unborn child in the womb.</b>

108
00:08:13.083 --> 00:08:15.083
<b>In family settings,</b>

109
00:08:15.083 --> 00:08:16.416
<b>usually,</b>

110
00:08:16.416 --> 00:08:21.958
<b>when someone's small desires begin to intensify,</b>

111
00:08:21.958 --> 00:08:24.958
<b>they often go unnoticed.</b>

112
00:08:24.958 --> 00:08:31.125
<b>These growing desires don't </b>
<b>significantly affect daily routines –</b>

113
00:08:31.125 --> 00:08:39.083
<b>which is why they seem harmless.</b>

114
00:08:39.083 --> 00:08:43.208
<b>They're like smoke covering fire,</b>

115
00:08:43.208 --> 00:08:47.791
<b>not heavily impacting the flame beneath.</b>

116
00:08:47.791 --> 00:08:55.666
<b>But if these desires keep intensifying, </b>
<b>there comes a time</b>

117
00:08:55.666 --> 00:09:02.416
<b>when someone in the family </b>
<b>becomes enslaved to them.</b>

118
00:09:02.416 --> 00:09:13.500
<b>These desires engulf that person like </b>
<b>a fetus in the womb – helpless,</b>

119
00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:22.791
<b>unable to see or do anything, </b>
<b>existing only in darkness.</b>

120
00:09:22.791 --> 00:09:26.000
<b>Take a small example –</b>

121
00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:37.625
<b>one day, busy parents turned on </b>
<b>a colorful show to distract their young child.</b>

122
00:09:37.625 --> 00:09:42.500
<b>It seemed harmless, completely innocent, right?</b>

123
00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:43.708
<b>Now,</b>

124
00:09:43.708 --> 00:09:47.250
<b>gradually, this became a habit,</b>

125
00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:52.166
<b>with the child insisting on </b>
<b>watching the same show again.</b>

126
00:09:52.166 --> 00:09:55.416
<b>The parents overlooked this change,</b>

127
00:09:55.416 --> 00:10:01.750
<b>and then eventually, this habit</b>

128
00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:03.541
<b>became an addiction.</b>

129
00:10:03.541 --> 00:10:12.208
<b>Now the child won't eat unless</b>
<b>that show is playing.</b>

130
00:10:12.208 --> 00:10:19.958
<b>And if parents refuse, the child rejects food.</b>

131
00:10:19.958 --> 00:10:23.083
<b>The child is helpless to their addiction,</b>

132
00:10:23.083 --> 00:10:27.791
<b>and the parents are helpless to</b>
<b>their child's behavior.</b>

133
00:10:27.791 --> 00:10:30.250
<b>A small desire</b>

134
00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:37.500
<b>that grew into stubbornness and finally addiction.</b>

135
00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:43.791
<b>Family elders must recognize </b>
<b>these growing desires early.</b>

136
00:10:43.791 --> 00:10:44.791
<b>Because</b>

137
00:10:44.791 --> 00:10:49.125
<b>they're easier to control at the initial stage.</b>

138
00:10:49.125 --> 00:10:50.333
<b>Moreover,</b>

139
00:10:50.333 --> 00:10:53.875
<b>families should have some discipline,</b>

140
00:10:53.875 --> 00:10:58.916
<b>some rules that elders follow themselves,</b>

141
00:10:58.916 --> 00:11:04.791
<b>so they can guide and </b>
<b>encourage younger children.</b>

142
00:11:04.791 --> 00:11:13.166
<b>Controlling intense desires will keep </b>
<b>family members' lives balanced and happy.</b>

143
00:11:13.166 --> 00:11:20.916
<b>This will build relationships based not </b>
<b>on dependencies, but on mutual love.</b>

144
00:11:20.916 --> 00:11:22.875
<b>This is the right way.</b>

145
00:11:22.875 --> 00:11:24.500
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

146
00:11:28.958 --> 00:11:34.541
<b>In an environment focused </b>
<b>solely on personal gain,</b>

147
00:11:34.541 --> 00:11:42.916
<b>mutual cooperation and </b>
<b>ethics gradually fade away.</b>

148
00:11:42.916 --> 00:11:46.875
<b>Imagine a workplace</b>

149
00:11:46.875 --> 00:11:53.166
<b>where there's fierce competition </b>
<b>for achieving targets, promotions, and such.</b>

150
00:11:53.166 --> 00:11:56.791
<b>Where only rivalry exists.</b>

151
00:11:56.791 --> 00:12:01.041
<b>The winner will gain immense recognition,</b>

152
00:12:01.041 --> 00:12:05.375
<b>while the loser might even lose their job.</b>

153
00:12:05.375 --> 00:12:09.208
<b>In such an environment, it's not unusual</b>

154
00:12:09.208 --> 00:12:15.833
<b>for people with intense desire</b>
<b>to win to adopt corrupt methods,</b>

155
00:12:15.833 --> 00:12:20.708
<b>while those desperately trying to avoid failure</b>

156
00:12:20.708 --> 00:12:26.916
<b>might attempt to pull others </b>
<b>down to save themselves.</b>

157
00:12:26.916 --> 00:12:29.166
<b>Now think,</b>

158
00:12:29.166 --> 00:12:32.125
<b>once someone becomes corrupt,</b>

159
00:12:32.125 --> 00:12:35.708
<b>can they break free from this trap?</b>

160
00:12:35.708 --> 00:12:36.708
<b>Because if</b>

161
00:12:36.708 --> 00:12:42.958
<b>they stop the corruption, </b>
<b>their past lies will be exposed.</b>

162
00:12:42.958 --> 00:12:49.041
<b>This is how desires trap humans in their grip.</b>

163
00:12:49.041 --> 00:12:52.041
<b>Once caught in the web,</b>

164
00:12:52.041 --> 00:12:54.250
<b>escape becomes difficult.</b>

165
00:12:54.250 --> 00:13:00.708
<b>The irony is that such desires </b>
<b>affect not just the individual,</b>

166
00:13:00.708 --> 00:13:01.666
<b>but</b>

167
00:13:01.666 --> 00:13:07.916
<b>the entire organization and other colleagues too. </b>

168
00:13:07.916 --> 00:13:11.708
<b>If someone succeeds through corrupt means,</b>

169
00:13:11.708 --> 00:13:17.041
<b>it encourages others to follow the same path.</b>

170
00:13:17.041 --> 00:13:24.791
<b>The organization's welfare lies</b>
<b>in senior officials recognizing</b>

171
00:13:24.791 --> 00:13:28.125
<b>and stopping such tendencies early.</b>

172
00:13:28.125 --> 00:13:29.416
<b>Otherwise,</b>

173
00:13:29.416 --> 00:13:35.791
<b>these layers of desire and unethical </b>
<b>behavior will keep growing thicker.</b>

174
00:13:35.791 --> 00:13:39.500
<b>This will only harm the organization.</b>

175
00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:44.875
<b>Those in leadership positions can </b>
<b>take several measures to remedy this:</b>

176
00:13:44.875 --> 00:13:46.208
<b>like</b>

177
00:13:46.208 --> 00:13:49.041
<b>Promote transparency</b>

178
00:13:49.041 --> 00:13:53.750
<b>Recognize and reward ethical conduct</b>

179
00:13:53.750 --> 00:14:02.916
<b>Include not just individual but also </b>
<b>group competitions, so people learn to cooperate</b>

180
00:14:02.916 --> 00:14:06.791
<b>Take strict action against corrupt behavior</b>

181
00:14:06.791 --> 00:14:08.666
<b>Through such measures,</b>

182
00:14:08.666 --> 00:14:16.458
<b>working people will understand that this </b>
<b>organization wants progress, but </b>

183
00:14:16.458 --> 00:14:23.125
<b>only and only hrough ethics </b>
<b>and mutual cooperation.</b>

184
00:14:23.125 --> 00:14:24.541
<b>Stay alert.</b>

185
00:14:24.541 --> 00:14:27.916
<b>Recognize desires in the workplace.</b>

186
00:14:27.916 --> 00:14:29.375
<b>Stop them.</b>

187
00:14:29.375 --> 00:14:33.166
<b>And remember to reflect deeply </b>
<b>on these teachings.</b>

